arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a logistics shipment tracker Blazor Web App. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-25cea5fdec5f47d8a96e8dc80b17f952/ShipmentTracker/` with:
- Server project: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/`
- Client project: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`
- Mode: Interactive Auto, Global with Individual authentication

## Architecture Rules (Auto mode)
- All interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Interactive components cannot access DbContext directly — use HTTP APIs
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient there, implement with EF Core on server
- Register matching services in both Program.cs files
- Identity/Account pages must stay static SSR (don't touch them)

## What to implement

### 1. Models (in `.Client` project, since both sides need them)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in `.Client` project)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 3. Client-side implementation (HttpClient-based, in `.Client` project)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
        => await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
}
```

### 4. Server-side implementation (EF Core, in server project)

Create `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentService(ApplicationDbContext db) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
        => await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
        => await db.Shipments.Where(s => s.CustomerEmail == customerEmail)
            .OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
            if (status == ShipmentStatus.Delivered)
                shipment.ActualDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow;
            await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }
    }
}
```

### 5. Update ApplicationDbContext to include Shipments

The existing DbContext is at `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`. Add a `DbSet<Shipment>` property:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
// ... existing usings

// Add inside the class:
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

### 6. API Endpoints

Add to `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Program.cs` BEFORE `app.Run();`:
```csharp
// Shipment API endpoints
var shipmentApi = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

shipmentApi.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
    Results.Ok(await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync()));

shipmentApi.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
{
    var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
    return shipment is not null ? Results.Ok(shipment) : Results.NotFound();
});

shipmentApi.MapGet("/customer/{email}", async (string email, IShipmentService service) =>
    Results.Ok(await service.GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(email)));

shipmentApi.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
{
    await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status);
    return Results.NoContent();
});
```

Add the required using at the top of Program.cs:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Services;
```

And register the server-side service in the server `Program.cs` (after `AddDatabaseDeveloperPageExceptionFilter`):
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentService>();
```

### 7. Update Client Program.cs

Register the HttpClient and client-side service:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress))
    .AddHttpMessageHandler<CookieHandler>();

// Fallback: use a simple scoped HttpClient
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

Actually, simplify the client Program.cs — just use a scoped HttpClient (the cookie is sent automatically in same-origin requests in WASM):
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 8. Pages (in `.Client` project)

**Delete** these template pages from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- `Counter.razor`
- `Weather.razor`

**Keep** `Home.razor` but replace its content.

**Replace `Home.razor`** with a landing page:
```razor
@page "/"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Tracker</h1>
<p>Welcome to the logistics shipment tracking system.</p>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <p>You are signed in as <strong>@context.User.Identity?.Name</strong>.</p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-3 mt-3">
            <a href="dispatcher" class="btn btn-primary">Dispatcher Dashboard</a>
            <a href="track" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Track a Shipment</a>
            <a href="my-shipments" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">My Shipments</a>
        </div>
    </Authorized>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <p>Please <a href="Account/Login">sign in</a> to track your shipments.</p>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
```

**Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Dispatcher.razor`** — Dispatcher dashboard showing all shipments with filtering and status update:
```razor
@page "/dispatcher"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@attribute [Authorize]
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>Dispatcher Dashboard</PageTitle>

<h1>Dispatcher Dashboard</h1>

<div class="mb-3">
    <input type="text" class="form-control" placeholder="Filter by destination..."
           @bind="filterText" @bind:event="oninput" />
</div>

@if (shipments is null)
{
    <p>Loading shipments...</p>
}
else if (!FilteredShipments.Any())
{
    <p>No shipments found.</p>
}
else
{
    <table class="table table-striped">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Tracking #</th>
                <th>Origin</th>
                <th>Destination</th>
                <th>Status</th>
                <th>Shipped</th>
                <th>Est. Delivery</th>
                <th>Actions</th>
            </tr>
